WEBVTT

00:00:00.267 --> 00:00:03.800
Prepare for the journey in your hut.

00:00:04.267 --> 00:00:07.800
Search the stores for food. Supplies are finite.

00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:11.800
Carry fuel to keep a stove burning when you stop.

00:00:12.267 --> 00:00:16.600
Consult the field map and choose your next supply hut.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:20.500
[Wind across the open snow]

00:00:21.067 --> 00:00:24.667
[Footsteps in the snow] A line of prints leads back across the slope.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:31.767 line:10% size:70%
Adler (on screen)  “Along the ridge to the next hut, while the weather holds. There should be oil in its store.”

00:00:32.033 --> 00:00:34.100
The ice bows underfoot.

00:00:34.233 --> 00:00:37.700
[Ice cracks. A splash.]

00:00:37.833 --> 00:00:39.567
The explorer hauls themself back onto the ice.

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:43.633
[Wind rises] Powder streams off the roof.

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:55.100
Away from a hut, pitch your tent and make shelter.

00:00:55.567 --> 00:00:58.300
Fuel the tent burner to warm the shelter.

00:00:59.033 --> 00:01:04.000
The stove lights. Its glow reaches the floorboards.

00:01:06.767 --> 00:01:10.300
Keep warm through the night, then continue the journey.

00:01:10.767 --> 00:01:18.633
Later, a relief ship calls. The broadcast gives the rendezvous and its arrival window.

00:01:19.100 --> 00:01:24.733
Mark the coastal rendezvous and plan the journey to reach it in time.

